{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Temperature-Dependent Thermophysical Properties.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Temperature-Dependent Thermophysical Properties.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"temperature dependent thermophysical properties temperature dependent thermophysical properties","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Temperature-Dependent Thermophysical Properties.md","fileName":"Temperature-Dependent Thermophysical Properties.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Temperature-Dependent Thermophysical Properties","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 00:55\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Thermophysical Material Characterization]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Thermophysical Material Characterization","Thermal Model Uncertainty from Input Properties","cosmolheattransfermodels.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Temperature-Dependent Thermophysical Properties.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Temperature-Dependent Thermophysical Properties.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"temperature dependent thermophysical properties temperature dependent thermophysical properties","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Temperature-Dependent Thermophysical Properties.md","fileName":"Temperature-Dependent Thermophysical Properties.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Temperature-Dependent Thermophysical Properties","heading":"Temperature-Dependent Thermophysical Properties","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Density, conductivity, heat capacity, viscosity, and emissivity may change over the temperature range traversed by a model. Replacing those relationships with constants can hide feedback between the evolving temperature and the coefficients governing its evolution.\n\nTables, interpolation functions, or analytic functions can represent measured dependence